        "summary":  "BNY\u0027s CIO Leigh-Ann Russell explains how leadership discipline centered on \u0027coherence\u0027 ΓÇö connecting strategy to execution and technology to trust ΓÇö enables organizations to scale AI without fragmentation. BNY achieved 220 AI solutions in production and 140 digital employees through a CEO-led strategy combined with a centralized platform called Eliza.",
        "execSummary":  "BNY\u0027s AI scale story is a concrete playbook for enterprise leaders: 220 solutions in production and 140 digital employees did not happen through decentralized experimentation ΓÇö they required CEO-level commitment, a unified internal platform, and a discipline the CIO calls coherence, meaning every AI investment is traceable back to a strategic outcome. For support and operations leaders, the Eliza platform model is worth examining as a template for consolidating AI agent deployments under a single governed infrastructure rather than allowing point-solution sprawl. The key caveat is that coherence at this scale presupposes strong executive alignment; organizations where AI ownership is contested will struggle to replicate it.",
