        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "An Infosys report finds that 72% of organizations have scaled fewer than a quarter of their AI pilots successfully, and two-thirds struggle to measure AI\u0027s actual financial benefits. Companies feel competitive pressure to deploy AI quickly for short-term optics rather than pursuing transformative long-term initiatives, undermining true ROI realization.",
        "execSummary":  "The Infosys data makes the 2026 AI paradox explicit: organizations are accelerating AI investment while simultaneously admitting they cannot measure its financial return ΓÇö a dangerous combination that sets the stage for budget corrections or executive disillusionment in the next 12-18 months. For enterprise AI leaders, the 72% pilot-scaling failure rate is the most decision-relevant finding: it suggests the problem is not ideation or funding but the organizational infrastructure required to move from proof-of-concept to production at scale. Customer-support and operations leaders should use this data to push back on pressure for rapid expansion of unvalidated pilots and instead advocate for deeper investment in the handful of use cases already showing measurable outcomes. The risk of chasing short-term deployment metrics is embedding expensive, low-value AI infrastructure that is difficult to unwind.",
