        "date":  "2026-08-21",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "A Deloitte survey of 501 senior U.S. executives found that while 73% expect half their business processes to be redesigned around AI agents within four years, only 20% believe their organizations are actually prepared for this transformation. Key barriers include poorly documented processes, fragmented data and systems, and entrenched organizational habits.",
        "execSummary":  "The Deloitte gap ΓÇö 73% expecting AI agent-led process redesign but only 20% ready for it ΓÇö is the defining organizational risk of the current AI cycle, and for customer-support leaders it maps directly to the challenge of deploying autonomous agents in contact centers and service workflows where process documentation is often tacit rather than codified. The three barriers Deloitte identifies (undocumented processes, fragmented data, entrenched habits) are all solvable through deliberate investment, but each takes longer than a typical AI vendor\u0027s implementation timeline promises. The practical implication is that organizations should begin process documentation and data unification work now, ahead of agent deployment, rather than discovering these gaps during rollout. Leaders who treat agent readiness as purely a technology problem will land in the 80% that are not prepared.",
        "vendorLean":  "Deloitte ΓÇö findings from a Deloitte-sponsored survey; framing may align with Deloitte\u0027s AI transformation consulting practice.",
